## Install

1. Drop the `Scripts/` folder into your project's `Assets/`.
2. **Right-click in Project → Create → Audio → {{ s.name }} Bank** to create your bank asset.
3. **Right-click → Create → Audio → Cue** to create individual `AudioCue` assets.
   Assign an AudioClip, set `id`, `category`, and (optionally) an `AudioMixerGroup`.
4. Drag your cues into the bank's `cues` list.
5. Add a GameObject to your scene with a `{{ s.name }}AudioManager` component and
   assign the bank.

## API

```csharp
{{ s.name }}AudioManager.Instance.Play("door_close");
{{ s.name }}AudioManager.Instance.Play("explosion", worldPos: transform.position);
{{ s.name }}AudioManager.Instance.StopMusic();
```

{% if variant == "music_layers" %}
## Music layers

Add a `{{ s.name }}MusicLayers` component to a GameObject. Assign {{ s.layer_count }}
stem AudioClips. Call `PlayAll()` once to sync them, then `SetLayer(i, volume)` to
mix them in/out as gameplay state changes.
{% elif variant == "crossfade_zones" %}
## Crossfade zones

Add a `{{ s.name }}CrossfadeZone` component to any GameObject with a trigger
collider. Set `enterCueId` and `exitCueId` to ambient cues in the bank. The
crossfade duration is `{{ "%.2f"|format(s.crossfade_seconds) }}` seconds.
{% endif %}
